Subject: configure: recognise substrate* in shared-libs host_os case

ncurses 6.4's configure has a host_os dispatch at line 6389 that
gates whether shared libraries are buildable.  Without a branch
matching substrate, CC_SHARED_OPTS stays empty and the build
bails with "Shared libraries are not supported in this version."

Treat substrate* the same as linux*/gnu*/k*bsd*-gnu — same
ELF/ld.so model, same -shared / -Wl,-soname output convention.

---
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -6386,7 +6386,7 @@
 		fi
 		cf_cv_rm_so_locs=yes
 		;;
-	(linux*|gnu*|k*bsd*-gnu)
+	(linux*|gnu*|k*bsd*-gnu|substrate*)
 		if test "$DFT_LWR_MODEL" = "shared" && test -n "$LD_RPATH_OPT" ; then
 			LOCAL_LDFLAGS="${LD_RPATH_OPT}\$(LOCAL_LIBDIR)"
 			LOCAL_LDFLAGS2="$LOCAL_LDFLAGS"
